        "text": "I have created all the requested Python files in the current working directory with the necessary AWS integration code. Here are the files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] summarize_text.py - calls a hosted LLM to summarize long text\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] extract_json.py - calls a hosted LLM to extract structured JSON from text\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] answer_with_context.py - calls a hosted LLM to answer a question using provided context\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] stream_completion.py - streams partial output tokens from a hosted LLM\n5. [HELPER] model_client.py - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Hosted LLM Inference and Model-Family Selection\n6. [HELPER] model_models.py - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Hosted LLM Inference and Model-Family Selection\n7. [LATER-STEP] prompt_safety.py - Checks prompts and generated text for unsafe content\n8. [LATER-STEP] result_translate.py - Translates generated model output\n9. [LATER-STEP] output_embedding.py - Embeds model outputs for clustering or retrieval\n10. [LATER-STEP] spoken_brief.py - Generates a spoken brief from the model output\n\nEach scored implementation file uses AWS as the concrete external provider and makes it identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities.",
